        "label": "Quadratics keep both roots",
        "body": "A relation that is quadratic in the unknown — however it's arranged — solves with the quadratic formula and outputs **every real root** as a list: [−6, 6] here, never just the positive branch. A repeated root comes out as one value; no real root is **#SOLVE!**.",
        "width": 400,
        "height": 150
      }
    },
